<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕδρᾰνον</span></b> , τό, poet.
		form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕδρα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seat, abode, dwelling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πελασγῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					212
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				18.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕ. κόσμου</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				26.4
			</span></i>: mostly in pl., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				176
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				233
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pae.Delph.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Maiist.
				36
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ἄνα ἐξ ἑδράνων</span>
			rise from thy <i>rest</i> or <i>idleness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				192
			</span></i>; Trag. only in lyr. exc. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1128.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ ἑδράνων ἔρημος</span>, which is
			Stoic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>chair</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stay, support</i>, said of an anchor, in sg., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.28
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i>).</div>
